# GitHub Actions + Amazon ECR CI/CD

## About

In this project, I automated the Docker image build and push process using GitHub Actions and Amazon ECR.

In my previous ECR project, I built the Docker image locally from WSL and pushed it to ECR manually. That worked, but it was not a real CI/CD flow. In this project, I wanted to make the process closer to how teams actually work: push code to GitHub, let the workflow build the image, and store the image in a container registry automatically.

## What this project does

When I push changes to the `main` branch:

1. GitHub Actions starts the workflow
2. The workflow checks out the repository code
3. Docker builds an nginx image using the project Dockerfile
4. GitHub Actions authenticates to AWS using an IAM role and OIDC
5. The Docker image is tagged with the ECR repository URI
6. The image is pushed to Amazon ECR with the `latest` tag

